<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coptic Pope of Alexandria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Coptic Patriarch of Alexandria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Coptic Pope of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> is the patriarch and head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coptic-orthodox-church">Coptic Orthodox Church</a>, the Miaphysite church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> that separated from the Chalcedonian church after 451. The patriarchs consecrated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of the Christian kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and the metropolitans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, binding those churches to Alexandria. Since the 11th century the patriarchal seat has been in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coptic-pope-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="Coptic Pope of Alexandria" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OSCE Parliamentary Assembly · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tawadros_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
